[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OWASP/MCP-Security-Testing-Guide/issues/comments/6399483914","html_url":"https://github.com/OWASP/MCP-Security-Testing-Guide/pull/21#issuecomment-6399483914","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OWASP/MCP-Security-Testing-Guide/issues/21","id":6399483914,"node_id":"IC_kwDOSuRVDc8AAAABfXBgCg","user":{"login":"vermava","id":18599968,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4NTk5OTY4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/18599968?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/vermava","html_url":"https://github.com/vermava","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vermava/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vermava/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vermava/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vermava/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vermava/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vermava/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vermava/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vermava/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vermava/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-10-25T15:24:53Z","updated_at":"2026-10-25T15:24:53Z","body":"The three limits of a local pin are worth keeping, and the lab boundaries are right: no public-log entries, a non-standard envelope, and pseudocode rather than a tool command. The tools-spec sentence is accurate, and SEP-3140 was closed on 22 September 2026 without a merge so it can return through a working group. Please say that, so the close does not read as a rejection of the design.\r\n\r\nThis is a different change from the request on #18. That comment asked for MCPSTG-TOOL-07. #19 is that test. SUPP-06 proposes a signature and a public log the 2026-07-28 specification does not define.\r\n\r\nPlease change the verdicts before merge:\r\n\r\n- A client with no verifier is **Not tested** for this proposed control. Case (a) currently grades that client **Insecure** for storing a hash and continuing, which is what \"What to snapshot\" still tells the reader to do.\r\n- **Insecure** means the client claims to verify and then accepts a bad envelope: missing or invalid inclusion proof, unexpected signer, or a served digest that does not match the logged digest.\r\n- Case (f) should match \"What to snapshot.\" A prompt that stops and asks a person when the hash changes is the existing control, scored with SUPP-05 and TOOL-07. It is **Insecure** here only when the client claims a log check and then accepts the unlogged revision.\r\n- Case (b) is the positive control. If a valid logged revision is refused, record **Not tested** and do not score (c)–(f). Leave the re-approval prompt to SUPP-05, as the objectives already do.\r\n- Severity Medium until a mechanism exists. In the control matrix, mark rug pulls and provenance. Leave typosquatting, dependency confusion, and inventory blank, and mark malicious servers if first-contact verification stays in the test.\r\n\r\n#16 and #19 also move the count from 79 to 80, and #19 edits the same Tests line in 3.05. Expect a conflict there.\r\n\r\nHappy to review the next push.","author_association":"COLLABORATOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OWASP/MCP-Security-Testing-Guide/issues/comments/6399483914/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OWASP/MCP-Security-Testing-Guide/issues/comments/6399885152","html_url":"https://github.com/OWASP/MCP-Security-Testing-Guide/pull/21#issuecomment-6399885152","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OWASP/MCP-Security-Testing-Guide/issues/21","id":6399885152,"node_id":"IC_kwDOSuRVDc8AAAABfXZ_YA","user":{"login":"intelligent-ears","id":186805503,"node_id":"U_kgDOCyJs_w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/186805503?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/intelligent-ears","html_url":"https://github.com/intelligent-ears","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/intelligent-ears/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/intelligent-ears/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/intelligent-ears/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/intelligent-ears/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/intelligent-ears/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/intelligent-ears/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/intelligent-ears/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/intelligent-ears/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/intelligent-ears/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-10-25T16:02:15Z","updated_at":"2026-10-25T16:02:15Z","body":"Pushed the changes in one commit:\r\n\r\n- Not tested verdict for clients without a verifier. Insecure is now only for a client that claims to verify and then accepts a bad envelope.\r\n- (b) is the positive control and gates scoring of (c)–(f). Re-approval stays with SUPP-05.\r\n- (f) now matches What to snapshot. Stop-and-ask on a hash change is scored under SUPP-05/TOOL-07, not as Insecure here.\r\n- Severity is Medium in the table and the block.\r\n- Control-matrix row: malicious servers, rug pulls, provenance.\r\n- SEP-3140 is described as closed on 22 Sep 2026 without merge, able to return through a WG (checked closed_at via the API).\r\n- The \"Local pins are TOFU\" subsection now says the local hash plus stop-and-ask is still the baseline, and SUPP-06 is a proposed addition on top of it.\r\n\r\nNote: SUPP-06 refers to MCPSTG-TOOL-07 as plain text, since it lands with #19. Neither #16 nor #19 has merged yet. I'll rebase for the count and the 3.05 Tests line after they do, or link TOOL-07 once it exists.","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OWASP/MCP-Security-Testing-Guide/issues/comments/6399885152/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OWASP/MCP-Security-Testing-Guide/issues/comments/6516225129","html_url":"https://github.com/OWASP/MCP-Security-Testing-Guide/pull/21#issuecomment-6516225129","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OWASP/MCP-Security-Testing-Guide/issues/21","id":6516225129,"node_id":"IC_kwDOSuRVDc8AAAABhGW0aQ","user":{"login":"alexar76","id":86793359,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg2NzkzMzU5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/86793359?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexar76","html_url":"https://github.com/alexar76","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexar76/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexar76/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexar76/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexar76/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexar76/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexar76/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexar76/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexar76/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexar76/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-10-30T06:07:41Z","updated_at":"2026-10-30T06:07:41Z","body":"A running instance of most of this model exists, which may help with the fixtures and the \"Tools\" list, so here is what it does and does not cover.\n\nHISTOR (https://histor.modelmarket.dev) is a public, append-only log of the tool definitions that servers listed in the official MCP registry actually serve. Each observation of a server's `tools/list` becomes a signed label; labels are leaves of an RFC 9162 Merkle tree with a signed tree head (Ed25519, `did:key`), and the API serves inclusion and consistency proofs. As of 2026-10-30: 1,281,508 leaves, 88,393 listed targets, 14,168 of them with at least one recorded change, 33,834 changes in the last 30 days. Audit procedure with nothing but the log's public key: https://github.com/alexar76/histor/blob/main/docs/log.md. Weekly snapshots, CC BY 4.0: doi:10.5281/zenodo.23512759.\n\nWhere it matches the test and where it does not, stated plainly:\n\n- **Logged revisions, split view, runtime drift (cases c, e, f):** covered. The log records what a server served the log's own reader; `POST /api/v1/check` takes the tools a client received and answers, signed, whether that set matches what the log has for the server. Two clients comparing their served digests against the log is exactly case (e).\n- **Publisher signature and signer identity (cases a, d):** not covered. HISTOR has no publisher signatures. The publisher side is a *declaration*: a publisher names the digests of the tool sets it ships in the `_meta` block of its registry `server.json` (bound to the namespace the registry verified) or in a file on its own domain. That is identity by namespace, not by key, and it is weaker than what SUPP-06 asks for. So a client using HISTOR as `<LAB_TLOG>` would be **Not tested** on (a) and (d) and scoreable on (c), (e), (f).\n\nTwo things from running it that may be worth a sentence in the test:\n\n1. **Canonical form.** We also use RFC 8785 + SHA-256, but over the tool entries normalised to `name`, `description`, `inputSchema`, `outputSchema`, sorted by name in UTF-16 code-unit order, not over an object keyed by name with `title` and `annotations`. Either is fine; the point is that both sides of the positive control (b) must agree before the test is run, or (b) fails for reasons that have nothing to do with the client. One concrete trap: a schema with a fractional number. JCS defines number serialisation, but not every JSON library follows it, so two implementations can produce two digests for one `tools/list`. We refuse to digest such a set at all rather than commit to bytes nobody else can reproduce. A fixture with `0.5` in a schema is a good negative control for the tester's own tooling.\n2. **\"A legitimate update looks like a rug pull.\"** A log gives a base rate. Between 2026-09-24 and 2026-10-26, 5,192 of 10,887 remote servers (47.7%) served a different list at least once, and about half of all recorded changes are description text only. A client that stops on every change stops often; the log is what lets re-approval be a comparison against the publisher's recorded history instead of a judgement call.\n\nFor Appendix F, if a public instance is acceptable as an example of the \"transparency-log client\" row: the API gives `GET /api/v1/log/sth`, `/log/proof/inclusion`, `/log/proof/consistency`, `/labels/<id>/proof`, and `POST /api/v1/check`; the `aimarket-histor` package on PyPI has the same as a CLI and as an MCP server. The lab-only rule in Preconditions still stands: nothing in a test should be written to a public log, and HISTOR has no write path for third parties anyway.\n\nHappy to adjust any of the numbers above to a dated snapshot if the test would rather cite a fixed one.\n","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OWASP/MCP-Security-Testing-Guide/issues/comments/6516225129/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OWASP/MCP-Security-Testing-Guide/issues/comments/6750617469","html_url":"https://github.com/OWASP/MCP-Security-Testing-Guide/pull/21#issuecomment-6750617469","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OWASP/MCP-Security-Testing-Guide/issues/21","id":6750617469,"node_id":"IC_kwDOSuRVDc8AAAABkl4_fQ","user":{"login":"vermava","id":18599968,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4NTk5OTY4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/18599968?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/vermava","html_url":"https://github.com/vermava","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vermava/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vermava/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vermava/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vermava/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vermava/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vermava/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vermava/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vermava/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vermava/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-11-09T20:27:30Z","updated_at":"2026-11-09T20:27:30Z","body":"SUPP-06 is a different observation from TOOL-07. Please keep the three TOFU gaps. A client that only stores a hash and asks a person is the control 3.13 already recommends, so grade that Secure. Grade Insecure only when the client claims to verify a signature and accepts a bad envelope. No verifier is Not tested, using the label from #52. Please leave the severity at Medium until a public log exists, and leave re-approval on SUPP-05. I’ll merge after that verdict change.\r\n","author_association":"COLLABORATOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OWASP/MCP-Security-Testing-Guide/issues/comments/6750617469/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OWASP/MCP-Security-Testing-Guide/issues/comments/6770556880","html_url":"https://github.com/OWASP/MCP-Security-Testing-Guide/pull/21#issuecomment-6770556880","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OWASP/MCP-Security-Testing-Guide/issues/21","id":6770556880,"node_id":"IC_kwDOSuRVDc8AAAABk45_0A","user":{"login":"intelligent-ears","id":186805503,"node_id":"U_kgDOCyJs_w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/186805503?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/intelligent-ears","html_url":"https://github.com/intelligent-ears","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/intelligent-ears/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/intelligent-ears/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/intelligent-ears/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/intelligent-ears/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/intelligent-ears/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/intelligent-ears/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/intelligent-ears/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/intelligent-ears/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/intelligent-ears/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-11-10T14:53:25Z","updated_at":"2026-11-10T14:53:25Z","body":"Pushed the verdict change and rebased onto main (#52 and GW-04 had merged):\r\n\r\n- A client that stores a hash and asks a person on change is now Secure, in (a), (e) and (f). That's the 3.13 baseline, and the test records that the signature and log cases weren't exercised. (e) notes that split-view detection needs the log.\r\n- Insecure only when the client claims to verify a signature or log inclusion and then accepts a bad envelope.\r\n- Not tested uses the #52 label: no verifier and no hash-and-ask baseline, or the positive control (b) refuses a valid logged revision.\r\n- The three TOFU gaps are unchanged. Severity stays Medium, and re-approval stays on SUPP-05.\r\n- Test count bumped to 81 after the GW-04 merge.\r\n\r\nOne edge case to confirm: a client that stores a hash but accepts changes without asking is Not tested here, since it has no baseline and isn't a claimed verifier. It fails the baseline, which SUPP-05/TOOL-07 cover. Happy to word it differently if you'd prefer.","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OWASP/MCP-Security-Testing-Guide/issues/comments/6770556880/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]